WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.652
Lab 1 runs in the provider
notices folder of the examples,

3
00:00:04.652 --> 00:00:08.034
in PowerShell 7, against a
fictional tenant in G C C.

4
00:00:08.034 --> 00:00:13.314
Step one lists what Microsoft 365 needs:
three calls, and only two permissions,

5
00:00:13.314 --> 00:00:16.448
Service Message dot Read
dot All for the posts,

6
00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:21.563
and Service Health dot Read dot All for
the issues and the health overviews.

7
00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:24.862
All three are marked
verified, and nothing writes.

8
00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:30.416
Step two prints each cloud's Graph
host: the worldwide host for G C C with

9
00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:36.160
the Global environment, then the U S
Government hosts for GCC High and DoD.

10
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.947
Step three collects Microsoft
365 from the day-one fixtures,

11
00:00:40.947 --> 00:00:46.213
as of November ninth, 2026: six
notices, five open, two needing action.

12
00:00:46.213 --> 00:00:50.180
Three advisories, a change,
an incident and a retirement.
